# self_biting.fspy with the knowledge argued (tasks.org,
# aida-referents-anaphora-knowledge): self_biting_is_odd derives the attack
# on bites !z !z from a premise it presumes, ~bites !z !z. Placed at a
# reading, the instance keeps that presumption; a derivation defeats a
# bare presumption, so bites !donkey !donkey is OUT, and the second
# pronoun falls back to the farmer.
lk.
pipeline unfolded.
declare iota : type.
declare farmer, donkey : iota -> bool.
declare has, bites : iota -> iota -> bool.
argument a_farmer_has_a_donkey : [!farmer:iota,!donkey:iota] exists x:iota, exists y:iota, farmer [x] - ~donkey [y] - ~has [x] [y].
elim [!farmer].
elim [!donkey].
by default.
dixi.
argument he_bites_him : [?c:iota,?d:iota] exists x:iota, exists y:iota, bites [x] [y].
elim [?c].
elim [?d].
by default.
dixi.
counterargument self_biting_is_odd : [!z:iota] bites [!z] [!z].
cut (~bites [!z] [!z]) n.
by default.
next.
elim n.
axiom.
dixi.
